---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Quality Criteria &amp; Selection Engine — AI Tools Hub"
  description="Transparent explanation of the 3-layer selection engine, automated gates, and anti-fake-star defense."
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12">
    <!-- Header -->
    <header class="border-b border-slate-200 pb-8 mb-10">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold border border-emerald-200 bg-emerald-50 text-emerald-800 mb-4 shadow-xs">
        <span>Transparent &amp; Deterministic</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 tracking-tight">
        Repo Quality Criteria &amp; Selection Engine
      </h1>
      <p class="text-base text-slate-600 mt-3 leading-relaxed">
        Why trust our directory? Entries are selected automatically by public rules. Nothing here is hand-tested. Every single entry is filtered and scored through our automated 3-layer selection engine. Zero pay-for-placement, zero unmaintained repos.
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- Architecture Overview -->
    <section class="space-y-12 text-slate-700">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2.5">
          <span class="w-7 h-7 rounded-lg bg-blue-50 border border-blue-200 flex items-center justify-center text-blue-700 text-sm font-mono font-bold">1</span>
          <span>Layer 1: Hard Metadata Gates (G1 &ndash; G9)</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          Before any repository is scored or categorized, it must pass 9 non-negotiable metadata filters:
        </p>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-slate-200 shadow-xs">
          <table class="w-full text-left text-xs font-mono">
            <thead class="bg-slate-50 border-b border-slate-200 text-slate-700 uppercase text-[10px]">
              <tr>
                <th class="p-3">Gate</th>
                <th class="p-3">Rule</th>
                <th class="p-3 font-sans">Rationale</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-200 bg-white">
              <tr>
                <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-blue-700">G1</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-slate-900">archived == false</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-slate-600 font-sans">Eliminates abandoned or frozen repositories.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-blue-700">G2</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-slate-900">fork == false</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-slate-600 font-sans">Points to canonical upstream repositories only.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-blue-700">G3</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-slate-900">stars &ge; 100</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-slate-600 font-sans">Community adoption baseline (waived for official vendors).</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-blue-700">G4</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-slate-900">pushed_at &ge; now - 180d</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-slate-600 font-sans">Rejects tools unmaintained for over 6 months.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-blue-700">G5</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-slate-900">created_at &le; now - 14d</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-slate-600 font-sans">Spam incubation defense; prevents sudden astro-turfing.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-blue-700">G6</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-slate-900">has_description == true</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-slate-600 font-sans">Requires clear repo purpose in metadata.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-blue-700">G7</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-slate-900">has_readme == true</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-slate-600 font-sans">Ensures basic documentation exists for users.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-blue-700">G8</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-slate-900">license in OSI_ALLOWLIST</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-slate-600 font-sans">Ensures legally usable open-source licensing.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-blue-700">G9</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-slate-900">not_blocked == true</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-slate-600 font-sans">Honors curator blocklist in <code class="text-blue-700 bg-blue-50 border border-blue-200 px-1 py-0.2 rounded font-mono">data/overrides/block.yaml</code>.</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2.5">
          <span class="w-7 h-7 rounded-lg bg-teal-50 border border-teal-200 flex items-center justify-center text-teal-700 text-sm font-mono font-bold">2</span>
          <span>Layer 2: Type Check &amp; Verifiable Evidence</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          A repo claiming to be an MCP server, Agent Skill, or Developer Tool is never trusted by topic alone. Our engine inspects git trees for verifiable evidence:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2.5 text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
          <li><strong class="text-slate-900">1. MCP Servers (`mcp_server`):</strong> Must have verifiable SDK dependency (<code class="bg-blue-50 text-blue-700 border border-blue-200 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">@modelcontextprotocol/sdk</code>, Python <code class="bg-blue-50 text-blue-700 border border-blue-200 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">mcp</code> / <code class="bg-blue-50 text-blue-700 border border-blue-200 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">fastmcp</code>, Go/Rust SDKs), manifest entry points, or presence in the official MCP Registry.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-slate-900">2. Agent Skills (`agent_skill`):</strong> Must contain physical <code class="bg-teal-50 text-teal-700 border border-teal-200 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">SKILL.md</code> files with valid YAML frontmatter specifying procedural instructions and tooling. Sibling skills within monorepos are aggregated into clean Skill Packs.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-slate-900">3. Agent Tools &amp; Repos (`agent_tool`):</strong> Standalone autonomous agent frameworks, terminal CLIs, browser harnesses, and AI developer engines (<code class="bg-purple-50 text-purple-700 border border-purple-200 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">topic:ai-agents</code>, <code class="bg-purple-50 text-purple-700 border border-purple-200 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">topic:coding-agent</code>) with executable install targets (<code class="font-mono text-slate-800">npx</code>, <code class="font-mono text-slate-800">uvx</code>, <code class="font-mono text-slate-800">pip install</code>, <code class="font-mono text-slate-800">brew</code>, <code class="font-mono text-slate-800">git clone</code>).</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2.5">
          <span class="w-7 h-7 rounded-lg bg-indigo-50 border border-indigo-200 flex items-center justify-center text-indigo-700 text-sm font-mono font-bold">3</span>
          <span>Layer 3: Quality Scoring &amp; Anti-Fake Star Defense</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Composite quality scoring balances multiple signals to prevent star manipulation:
        </p>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 text-xs">
          <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-white border border-slate-200 shadow-xs">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2.5 text-sm">Composite Score Signals</h3>
            <ul class="space-y-1.5 text-slate-600">
              <li>&bull; Log-scaled star baseline (prevents hyper-stars from dwarfing peers)</li>
              <li>&bull; Push recency decay function</li>
              <li>&bull; Contributor breadth &amp; fork activity</li>
              <li>&bull; Official vendor bonus (+15 points)</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-white border border-slate-200 shadow-xs">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-rose-700 mb-2.5 text-sm">Anti-Fake Defense Triggers</h3>
            <ul class="space-y-1.5 text-slate-600">
              <li>&bull; Star burst anomaly (&gt;80% of stars in under 48h)</li>
              <li>&bull; Commit activity check (avoids zero-code star farms)</li>
              <li>&bull; Issue ratio check (abnormally low issue activity)</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2.5">
          <span class="w-7 h-7 rounded-lg bg-orange-50 border border-orange-200 flex items-center justify-center text-orange-700 text-sm font-mono font-bold">4</span>
          <span>Layer 4: Weekly Trend Velocity &amp; Momentum Radar</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Unlike all-time leaderboards where 100k-star giants remain permanently frozen at the top, our Weekly Trend Radar measures real 7-day developer velocity (&Delta;S<sub>7d</sub>) computed from historical Git snapshots in <code class="font-mono text-slate-800 bg-slate-100 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">data/signals/</code>.
        </p>
        <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-white border border-slate-200 shadow-xs text-xs space-y-3">
          <div>
            <span class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-sm block mb-1">Breakout Velocity Formula</span>
            <code class="block p-3 rounded-lg bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200 font-mono text-[11px] text-slate-800 overflow-x-auto">
              TrendingScore = &Delta;S<sub>7d</sub> &times; (1 + min(2.0, &Delta;S<sub>7d</sub> / max(S<sub>t-1</sub>, 250)))
            </code>
          </div>
          <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
            This formula rewards both absolute star volume (&Delta;S<sub>7d</sub>) and percentage growth velocity (&Delta;S<sub>7d</sub> / S<sub>t-1</sub>), giving rising newcomers a fair chance to compete against massive incumbents.
          </p>
          <div class="pt-2 border-t border-slate-100">
            <span class="font-bold text-slate-900 block mb-1">Anti-Sybil &amp; Isolation Safeguards:</span>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-slate-600">
              <li><strong>Non-Negative Clamping:</strong> &Delta;S<sub>7d</sub> = max(0, S<sub>t</sub> - S<sub>t-1</sub>) prevents star revocation glitches from corrupting ranks.</li>
              <li><strong>Synthetic Age Velocity Quarantine:</strong> Genuinely new repos without historical baseline data are quarantined from dominating the weekly top 25 until 7 days of real velocity have been observed.</li>
              <li><strong>Monorepo Sub-Skill Quarantine:</strong> Only primary repository entries (<code class="font-mono">is_pack_primary === true</code>) qualify for leaderboard ranking, preventing multi-skill repos from filling all 25 top spots.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
